This tool writes configuration to live industrial equipment. That warranty disclaimer is not
boilerplate: read the safety rules in CLAUDE.md, and satisfy yourself about what a build does
before pointing it at a plant network.

---

This project is built from public specifications - RFC 951, RFC 1542, RFC 2131, RFC 2132, RFC 1350,
RFC 2347/2348/2349, RFC 7440, and ODVA's published CIP and EtherNet/IP documentation. No part of it
is derived from decompiling the Rockwell BOOTP/DHCP tool or from Wireshark's GPL-licensed
dissectors.

Third-party components are used under their own licences:

  - CommunityToolkit.Mvvm       - MIT
  - Microsoft.Data.Sqlite       - MIT
  - SQLitePCLRaw               - Apache-2.0
  - SQLite itself               - public domain
  - xUnit (tests only)          - Apache-2.0

src/NetControl.Core/Oui/oui.bin is a repacking of the IEEE public MA-L, MA-M, MA-S and IAB
registries, which IEEE publishes for public use.
